# /etc/cron.d/wax — scheduled maintenance for the Wax/Musicography app.
# See lib/cron/README.md for install / uninstall / verify instructions.
#
# Format note: /etc/cron.d/ entries take a username column (between the
# schedule and the command). This file uses `root` because both pipx (which
# installs yt-dlp/spotdl into /root/.local/) and the project venv at
# /var/www/download-music-wed/.venv-ytmusic/ are owned by root today. If
# that changes (see TODO #8 "don't run as root"), update the user column.
#
# Disk cleanup of music/ and playlists/ is NOT here — it runs in-process from
# lib/disk-cleanup.ts on a 6-hour interval. The orchestrator bootstraps it on
# first job creation so reboots reset the timer naturally.

# Cron's default PATH is minimal; explicitly include the dirs where pipx and
# /usr/bin live so the commands below resolve without absolute paths everywhere.
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# ── Weekly: upgrade pipx-installed CLIs (yt-dlp, spotdl) ─────────────────────
# YouTube breaks yt-dlp extractors every few weeks. Auto-upgrade catches the
# fixes before users see "Sign in to confirm you're not a bot" errors.
0 4 * * 1 root /usr/bin/pipx upgrade-all >>/var/log/wax/pipx-upgrade.log 2>&1

# ── Weekly: upgrade ytmusicapi inside the project venv ──────────────────────
# Offset by 15 min so the two pip operations don't fight for the network.
# Targets the project-local venv created by first-time setup; do NOT switch to
# `pip install --user` — that would shadow the venv install at runtime.
15 4 * * 1 root /var/www/download-music-wed/.venv-ytmusic/bin/pip install --upgrade ytmusicapi >>/var/log/wax/ytmusicapi-upgrade.log 2>&1

# ── Every 6 hours: cookie health check ──────────────────────────────────────
# Dry-runs yt-dlp against a stable videoId. If YouTube returns "Sign in to
# confirm you're not a bot", pings COOKIE_ALERT_WEBHOOK (Discord/Slack URL)
# so the cookies file can be refreshed promptly. Silent if no webhook is
# configured. Logs to /var/log/wax/check-cookies.log for post-mortem.
0 */6 * * * root /var/www/download-music-wed/lib/cron/check-cookies.sh >>/var/log/wax/check-cookies.log 2>&1
